# RSF02-06: the order in which the shield looks at a query string.
title A query parameter is checked against its type first; only free text meets the attack patterns
row  req:box "?q=<script>…" "a request with a query" | known:warnbox "Known parameters" "typed: int, word, id, text" | patterns:warnbox "Attack patterns" "free text only, decoded twice" | site:okbox "Your site"
row  unknown:nobox "404" "unknown, or not of its type" | attack:nobox "403" "an attack pattern, named"
arrow req -> known
arrow known -> patterns "text"
arrow patterns -> site "clean" go
arrow known -> unknown "wrong"
arrow patterns -> attack "a hit"
note A number or a word cannot carry an attack: the patterns never look at it.
